{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2023",
    "lib": ["ES2023"],
    "module": "NodeNext",
    "moduleResolution": "NodeNext",
    "rootDir": "src",
    "outDir": "dist",

    "strict": true,
    /*
      Dead code is not free here, because `verbatimModuleSyntax` below keeps import
      statements exactly as written: an import nobody reads is still emitted, still resolved
      at startup, and still shipped. Four of them were — `node:crypto`, `createReadStream`,
      `pipeline` and `node:events`, left behind when the checksum machinery moved into the
      reader — along with a `rowsIn` helper that had a doc comment and no callers.

      Not `noUnusedParameters`: the codebase names a deliberately unused argument `unused`
      rather than `_unused`, which that check does not accept, and renaming twenty callbacks
      to satisfy it would be the tail wagging the dog.
    */
    "noUnusedLocals": true,
    "noUncheckedIndexedAccess": true,
    "noImplicitOverride": true,
    "noFallthroughCasesInSwitch": true,
    "exactOptionalPropertyTypes": true,
    "verbatimModuleSyntax": true,
    "isolatedModules": true,

    "declaration": true,
    /*
      Off, because a declaration map can only point at source the package does not ship.

      `files` is ["dist", ...] on purpose, and `inlineSources` puts the TypeScript inside the
      .js.map so a stack trace resolves in an installed copy. TypeScript has no equivalent for
      declaration maps: every .d.ts.map shipped said `"sources": ["../src/index.ts"]` with no
      `sourcesContent`, so "Go to Definition" in a consumer's editor followed it to a path
      that is not there. Without the map the same jump lands in the .d.ts, which is accurate
      and present.
    */
    "declarationMap": false,
    "sourceMap": true,
    // Sources embedded in the maps, because src/ is not in the published package and a map
    // pointing at ../src/cli.ts resolves to nothing once installed. A stack frame inside
    // edf2csv should land on the line that produced it, not on a missing file.
    "inlineSources": true,
    "removeComments": false,
    "newLine": "lf",

    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "forceConsistentCasingInFileNames": true
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*.ts"],
  "exclude": ["node_modules", "dist", "test"]
}
